<p>
  From then on, Save all tabs in the tabs panel does what the OneTab button did, except that the
  tabs land in groups you name, next to your notes and to-dos.
</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<h3>Does importing change anything in OneTab?</h3>
<p>No. TabCabin only reads the file, so keep OneTab until you are happy with the boards.</p>
<h3>Can I import a newer export later?</h3>
<p>Yes. Every import goes into a new workspace, so nothing you already have is overwritten.</p>
<h3>What else does TabCabin have that OneTab doesn't?</h3>
<p>
  Notes, to-dos and reminders next to links, search across everything, and sync between your
  computers when you sign in. The <a href="/alternatives/onetab/">OneTab comparison</a> has the full
  table.
</p>
